## Model Conventions

Models live in `app/models/`. Rules:
- Use SQLAlchemy 2.0 style: `Mapped[type]` / `mapped_column()`
- Every multi-tenant model has `account_id: Mapped[int]` (FK to accounts)
- Every model implements `to_dict()` for API serialization
- Soft deletes via `archived_at` / `is_archived` pattern (not hard deletes)

```python
class Job(Base):
    __tablename__ = "jobs"

    id: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(primary_key=True)
    account_id: Mapped[int] = mapped_column(ForeignKey("accounts.id"), nullable=False)
    title: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(255), nullable=False)
    status: Mapped[str] = mapped_column(String(50), default="draft")
    archived_at: Mapped[datetime | None] = mapped_column(nullable=True)
    created_at: Mapped[datetime] = mapped_column(default=func.now())
    updated_at: Mapped[datetime] = mapped_column(onupdate=func.now())

    def to_dict(self) -> dict:
        return {
            "id": self.id,
            "title": self.title,
            "status": self.status,
            ...
        }
```

