## Celery Background Jobs (`app/jobs/`)

Workers process async tasks. Key jobs:

| Job | Trigger | Purpose |
|-----|---------|---------|
| `deliver_esign_package` | Stage change or manual request | Merge HTML template, generate PDF, send to candidate |
| `sync_label_search` | Label create/update | Keep search index in sync |
| `flush_audit_buffer` | Celery Beat (scheduled) | Flush Redis-buffered audit events → PostgreSQL |
| `send_email` | Various | Outbound email via configured channel |

**Inline fallback:** If Redis/Celery is unavailable, some paths execute the task inline synchronously.

Beat schedule defined in `config/schedule.py`. Worker command: `python manage.py worker`.

