## E-Sign Flow (End-to-End)

```
Recruiter creates template (HTML with merge tags) in Settings > E-Sign Templates
   ↓
Recruiter creates stage rule: "when candidate enters Offer stage → send template X"
   ↓
Candidate moves to that pipeline stage
   ↓
AuditLogMiddleware or stage-change service fires → enqueues deliver_esign_package Celery task
   ↓
Worker: merges HTML template with candidate data, generates PDF (WeasyPrint/fpdf2),
        creates SigningRequest with unique token, emails candidate
   ↓
Candidate opens tokenized URL (/public/esign/:token) — no login required
   ↓
Candidate reviews, enters legal name, signs → POST /public/esign/:token/sign
   ↓
Worker generates final signed PDF, stores in ESIGN_ARTIFACTS_DIR
   ↓
Candidate downloads PDF; recruiter sees status in candidate record and signed docs library
```

---

## Audit Log Flow

- `AuditLogMiddleware` captures every mutating request (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE)
- If `AUDIT_LOG_BUFFER_ENABLED=true`: events written to Redis list
- Celery Beat runs `flush_audit_buffer` on schedule → batch-inserts to `audit_logs` table
- If Redis unavailable: events written directly to PostgreSQL synchronously
- Recruiters browse via Settings > Audit & Compliance (`GET /api/v1/audit/logs`)

